# Orchestrator: SDD

Purpose:
  Thin reference to the chain execution engine.
  The actual orchestration logic lives in chains/ and workflow/.
  This file exists for backward compatibility only.

Modes:
  AUTO — AI decides low-risk items
  SUPERVISED — AI recommends, human approves major decisions
  STRICT — Human approval required for architecture, security, DB migration, release
  AUDIT — Analysis only, no modifications
  READ_ONLY — Project analysis, no code changes

Execution:
  All execution flows through the chain graph (chains/INDEX.sdd).
  The orchestrator selects chains, applies policies, and executes stages.

Navigation:
  Chains: @../chains/INDEX.sdd
  Workflow: @../workflow/INDEX.sdd
  Agent: @../agent/INDEX.sdd
  Policies: @../workflow/policies.sdd

Rules:
  [OD1] All execution MUST go through the chain graph.
  [OD2] Policy engine enforces authorization before execution.
  [OD3] Human gates are mandatory for critical actions.
  [OD4] Token economy rules apply to all execution.

State: +
